    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d81">

                <pb facs="0166" n="154" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg154"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EAC/53</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the United Kingdom
                            Representative to the European Advisory Commission</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Strang</hi>)<anchor
                        n="71" xml:id="d81-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">E.A.C. (44) 3</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-15">15 January,
                        1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Allied Control Machinery in Germany during the
                        period of Occupation</hi>
                </p>
                <p>In compliance with the invitation issued to Delegations by the European Advisory
                    Commission at its first meeting on January 14th, I circulate to my colleagues,
                    for the consideration of the Commission, some proposals on the Allied control
                    machinery which would operate in Germany during the period of occupation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W[<hi rendition="#small-caps">illiam</hi>] S[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >trang</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d81-a1.xml" xpointer="d81-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d81-f1" n="71" type="source" xml:id="d81-f1-content">
                <p>Copy transmitted to the Department by the Ambassador in the United Kingdom in his
                    despatch 13325, January 15; received January 20.</p>
            </note>
